      "narration": "Why is the sky blue, if sunlight is white?",
      "on_screen_text": "Why is the sky blue?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "blue?"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cielo_prism",
      "narration": "White light actually carries every color mixed together, as a prism shows.",
      "on_screen_text": "White = every color",
      "highlight_words": [
        "color"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cielo_molecules",
      "narration": "When it enters the atmosphere, that light hits tiny air molecules, mostly nitrogen and oxygen.",
      "on_screen_text": "It hits the air",
      "highlight_words": [
        "air"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cielo_scatter",
      "narration": "And those molecules scatter blue light much more than red: they bounce it in every direction.",
      "on_screen_text": "Blue bounces",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Blue"
      ],
      "sfx": "pop",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cielo_everywhere",
      "narration": "That's why, wherever you look, blue light reaches you from the whole sky.",
      "on_screen_text": "Blue from everywhere",
      "highlight_words": [
        "everywhere"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cielo_violet",
      "narration": "And violet, which scatters even more? There's less of it in sunlight, and our eyes are far more sensitive to blue.",
      "on_screen_text": "What about violet?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "violet?"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "cielo_sunset",
      "narration": "At sunset, light crosses much more atmosphere: the blue gets lost along the way and the oranges and reds come through.",
      "on_screen_text": "Sunset: a long path",
      "highlight_words": [
        "long"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
