  "description": "Sunlight carries every color. Air molecules scatter short-wavelength (blue) light much more than long-wavelength (red) light: that's Rayleigh scattering. So blue reaches us from the whole sky, and at sunset, when light crosses more atmosphere, only oranges and reds get through. On the Moon, with no atmosphere, the sky is black. Original 3D animation.",
